# Line endings and file modes, pinned rather than left to each machine's git config.
#
# This repository is developed on Windows with `core.autocrlf=true` and
# `core.filemode=false`, and both defaults have already broken CI once: `gradlew` landed in
# the index as 100644 instead of 100755 and every job failed with
# `./gradlew: Permission denied` (exit 126). The mode is fixed with
# `git update-index --chmod=+x gradlew`; the rules below stop the line-ending half of the
# same problem, where a CRLF `gradlew` fails on a Linux runner with `bad interpreter`.

# Let git decide for text, but never guess for the files below.
* text=auto

# Shell scripts must be LF on every platform: the shebang is read byte-for-byte.
*.sh            text eol=lf
gradlew         text eol=lf

# Windows batch files must be CRLF: cmd.exe mis-parses LF-only .bat labels and gotos.
*.bat           text eol=crlf
*.cmd           text eol=crlf

# Never touched. Some of these are the AS3 original's assets, which must stay byte-identical
# to what `tools/import_card_art.py` copies out of `sources/`.
*.png           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.jpeg          binary
*.gif           binary
*.jar           binary
*.apk           binary
*.swf           binary
*.air           binary
*.p12           binary
*.keystore      binary
*.jks           binary
